{"title": "Stop first, size second", "type": "One trick", "hooks": ["Don't size your trade first. Place the stop, then size it.", "Size your trade from the stop, never the other way round.", "Stop hiding your stop a hair below your entry."], "scenes": [{"kind": "hook", "vo": "Don't size your trade first. Place the stop, then size it.", "text": "Stop first. Size second.", "chart": 0, "win": [20, 115], "show": 90}, {"kind": "question", "chart": 0, "badge": "Q", "head": "Where does the stop go?", "vo": "Yeti Frost Foods bounces off support, and you buy. Where's the stop? Just below support, a hair below the entry, or far below?", "win": [20, 115], "options": ["Just below the support, outside the usual noise", "A hair below the entry, to lose as little as possible", "Far below, so it is never hit"], "answer": 0, "show": 90, "cues": [{"say": "", "do": "options"}, {"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 289.58, "label": "Support", "tone": "level"}, {"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 290.06, "label": "Entry", "tone": "entry"}]}, {"kind": "answer", "chart": 0, "head": "Just below support", "vo": "Just below support, outside the usual noise. That's where the idea is proved wrong. Here it was hit after six candles, a planned loss.", "win": [20, 115], "reveal_to": 115, "carry": true, "cues": [{"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 288.18, "label": "Below support", "tone": "stop"}, {"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 289.71, "label": "Tight", "tone": "stop"}, {"say": "", "do": "line", "price": 276.07, "label": "Wide", "tone": "stop"}]}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Tight stops get hit by chance", "vo": "The tight stop was hit too, after six candles. A stop inside the normal noise gets hit by chance.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "big", "text": "Wide stops make tiny positions", "vo": "The far stop wasn't hit. But a stop that far makes each loss so big the position has to be tiny.", "chart": null}, {"kind": "outro", "text": "Stop first. Then size.", "vo": "So place the stop where you're wrong, then size the trade from it. Practise it at memestreet.net.", "chart": null}], "caption": "Don't size your trade first. Place the stop, then size it.\n\nA stop goes where the trade idea is proved wrong: here, just below the support.\nToo tight, and normal noise hits it by chance.\nToo wide, and the position has to be tiny.\n\nSave this for your next entry.\n\nPractise at memestreet.net\n\nFictional market. Not investment advice.\n\n#MemeStreet #StopLoss #RiskManagement #LearnToTrade", "charts": [{"candles": [[291.71, 291.82, 291.03, 291.8, 3146], [291.83, 292.0, 291.46, 291.48, 1972], [291.49, 291.9, 291.04, 291.79, 1666], [291.86, 292.91, 291.67, 292.48, 2142], [292.48, 292.6, 292.46, 292.6, 506], [292.6, 292.77, 291.91, 292.02, 662], [291.85, 295.66, 291.85, 294.66, 3391], [294.63, 295.17, 292.01, 292.76, 3623], [292.64, 293.19, 290.82, 291.42, 3504], [291.45, 294.38, 290.18, 293.84, 6102], [293.82, 293.87, 293.03, 293.44, 2232], [293.46, 293.97, 293.14, 293.43, 1382], [293.8, 294.13, 292.9, 293.62, 4005], [293.6, 294.77, 293.42, 294.1, 1930], [294.14, 294.34, 291.81, 291.99, 1669], [291.96, 293.93, 291.95, 293.79, 2411], [293.79, 294.0, 293.69, 293.86, 525], [293.86, 293.99, 293.74, 293.78, 412], [293.83, 293.95, 293.02, 293.33, 1744], [293.32, 293.62, 292.1, 293.53, 1866], [293.54, 297.35, 293.54, 297.35, 1830], [297.32, 297.36, 296.05, 296.71, 1325], [296.69, 298.47, 296.38, 298.38, 1738], [298.44, 298.85, 297.98, 298.21, 1793], [297.97, 299.88, 297.97, 299.77, 9697], [299.6, 300.83, 298.28, 299.41, 5685], [299.63, 300.32, 297.4, 299.31, 9326], [299.57, 300.13, 298.75, 299.28, 6370], [299.29, 299.39, 298.89, 299.19, 1509], [299.19, 299.38, 298.92, 299.0, 1216], [299.39, 300.29, 297.14, 297.44, 10207], [297.47, 297.75, 292.86, 293.69, 12249], [293.62, 293.62, 289.16, 289.16, 11621], [289.19, 290.43, 283.56, 283.56, 27732], [283.51, 283.8, 282.67, 283.18, 4969], [283.21, 283.51, 282.52, 283.41, 5289], [282.64, 286.22, 281.59, 285.98, 14462], [286.02, 287.47, 284.15